  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-21T21:47:03.370Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently if you are a group owner or admin, You can view, close, moderate instances, One of the biggest struggles is correctly moderating users who open innappropirate instances.\n\nLets take for example your a SFW group and someone opens a NSFW world, Thats clearly not allowed, In order to correctly moderate the adminstriative people need to handle this, Currently the extensive manor is going into the groups Audit log and checking that way.\n\nAudit logs can get very extensive and offen flooded after just 2 hours have past making it difficult to find if your groups super active.\n\nCurrently \"creatorId\" is only exposed to the Creator of the instance themselfs.\n\nI request that \"creatorId\" be exposed to group administrative permission such as \"manage instance\" permission, this can Heavily reduce the API call rate of custom bots lowering VRChats infstructure load and allows groups to better moderate bad actors.",
